# Phase 7.5 BUILD-B — Stage B PASS (OptiPlex silicon): the Phase-4 stack over a
# real USB-Ethernet dongle on bare metal.
# Scenario: usb_ethernet_baremetal (blind hardware — NVMe NEO_LOG_v1 sink at
#           0x10000000, no JTAG/debugger; this is the extracted sink).
# Date: 2026-06-12. Branch: codex/phase-7.5-build-B-usb-ethernet-jarvis.
# Host: Dell OptiPlex 7080, Intel xHCI root port. ISO sha256
#       1708ed4585f46d4d4341c868d9a2f877558bdecc920040585959f8cc1b5bc473.
# Adapter: UGREEN AX88179 USB-GbE (0b95:1790), gigabit copper to the LAN.
#
# What this run proves (ISC-15/16, ADR-047, ANSPEC §10.7):
# - Real-device enumeration on silicon: the AX88179 exposes 3 configs; the
#   driver picks cfg3 (CDC-ECM, class 02/06) BY CONTENT — skipping cfg1 (vendor
#   0xFF native ASIX) and cfg2 (NCM 02/0D) — and claims it via the 7.5-A seam.
#   (Two other devices on the bus — a Realtek 0bda:c811 USB-WiFi and the Intel
#   AX201 BT 8087:0026 — are correctly NOT bound: no ECM function.)
# - AX88179 native TX bring-up in cfg1 before the ECM switch: AX88179_PHY
#   physr=0xa400 decodes LINK-UP + GIGABIT + FULL-DUPLEX (0x0400|0x8000|0x2000);
#   fifo=0x00000000 means the link_reset TX-FIFO-ready handshake armed transmit
#   (bit 0x40000000 clear); bind_fail=None (the deconfigure→cfg3 path is clean).
# - The CDC-ECM driver transmits RAW Ethernet frames (per spec — the ASIX TX
#   header was a disproven detour that corrupted cfg3 TX and was removed).
# - REAL DORA over the bulk pipes → a REAL LAN lease: <optiplex-ip> /24, router
#   <router-ip>, dns <dns-ip>; offer=1 ack=1 and a DNS round-trip (udp53=1).
#   Independently wire-confirmed by a netsh/etl2pcapng capture on the segment:
#   the full DISCOVER/OFFER/REQUEST/ACK + a post-lease gratuitous ARP.
# - The unlock was a NeoPlutarch DHCP-client fix (BOOTP chaddr was empty +
#   broadcast flag clear — real servers drop that; QEMU/slirp had masked it).
# - I-14(c1) intact on the device's live DMA: fence_admits=322 fence_refusals=0.
#
# net/kernel diff for the data path stayed empty — the Phase-4 stack ran
# unmodified over USB; only the AX88179 vendor TX bring-up + the DHCP chaddr fix
# were added. extract: BUILD-5b neo-extract-log path / dd of the 0x10000000 sink.

